From 437d6ced66aae416258ba44abc175c731a396d55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:57:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Read the service index and platform host policy through
 the local verifier when chosen

verified-chain.mjs: one proof-backed snapshot per read from the local verifier
(loopback only): a confirmed block, fresh, monotonic, header re-checked, pinned
client with proof-backed methods only, quorum-class error codes, and ONE
referenced deadline over the whole operation including the caller's callback,
after which the pinned client refuses. The service index (readServiceIndex and
native control candidates via indexAuthority/indexRead) and the platform host
policy (hostPolicySnapshot, verifiedHostSnapshot, createHostPolicyRuntime) use
it when chainAuthority is 'verifier'; then no provider client is built, so a
refusal never falls back. Cold discovery, index and policy carriers, the host
services runner and policy-mirror role, gate carriers, the storage-indexer
registry read, native control and lease relay discovery all follow the
configured authority (config keys or ENCLAVE_CHAIN_AUTHORITY /
ENCLAVE_CHAIN_VERIFIER). Quorum stays the default; the gate's decisions and the
measured gate's configured grace are unchanged.
